Z||000000||HEFTY13||01-06-2000||03:43 PM||||My 87 GT isn't liking the Ohio winter. It'll start fine in the morning and afternoon, when I go to leave work around 6 pm, no start. It cranks fine, just won't fire up. This has been going on for two days. When it runs, it runs strong. Any suggestions ? I'm thinking dist cap or fuel filter. I just tried to start it after sitting for an hour, no start. HELP !!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||deceler8||01-06-2000||04:07 PM||||Might be time for new plug wires.<P>If snow gets on them through the deck lid vents, it may cause misfiring. <P>Snow seems to cause this problem more than rain as the snow is able to blow around to areas that rain can't reach. Also, things dry out slower in the winter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-06-2000||04:12 PM||||When it won't start after work what do you do? Do you leave it until morning when it starts up ok?||||reg||1
Z||000003||wwh0001||01-06-2000||04:21 PM||||No start but cranks good. Either not getting fuel or no spark. Easy to test for spark. When it won't start have someone crank engine, have one spark plug wire off and place next to something metal and see if a spark is there.<BR>If this is an auto and wont start when in park, shift to neutral. If it starts then it is probably your pick up coil.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||HEFTY13||01-06-2000||04:56 PM||||I let it sit overnight at work, It is a manual trans. Coil ? When it does start, it fires up on the first crank. Even when it doesn't start I hear the fuel pump start. When it's running, it's strong. It's got be baffled. I'm going to try the coil, cap & rotor.||||reg||1
